WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.868
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.767
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.167
Thank you for watching at home.
Thank you for being here again.

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:11.067
Well, guys, we're right in the
middle of the holiday season.

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:13.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Do you feel the vibes?

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.801
And if you're waiting to buy
a Christmas tree,

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.667
you better hurry, because due to
high demand and low supply,

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.567
prices are soaring.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.167
Yeah.
I'm trying to get ahead of this.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.601
That's why every night,
on the way home,

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:24.734
I cut one branch off

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.434
the Rockefeller Center
Christmas Tree.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.434
I just take it away from there.

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:31.334
I'm getting there.

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:34.734
♪ Christmastime ♪

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.133
Yeah, it's the holiday season,

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.267
and today, New York
got an early Christmas gift.

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:40.868
Aaron Judge is coming back
to the Yankees!

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.267
Yes!

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.200
That's right.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:51.434
Yankees superstar Aaron Judge
has decided to stay in New York,

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.367
agreeing to a nine-year,
$360 million contract.

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:59.601
When he heard that,
Babe Ruth said, "What the hell?

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:03.834
I got paid in peanuts and
Cracker Jacks."

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.601
$360 million.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.601
Today, Judge walked into
the owner's office and said,

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:09.667
"You're in my seat."

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:10.767
What a deal.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:12.133
Aaron is now the only person

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.767
who can afford a beer
in Yankee Stadium.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.968
-Oh!
-Yeah.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.567
It's true.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.868
The good news is,
Judge got $360 million.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.467
The bad news is,
the rest of the team

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.601
is now getting paid in crypto.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.200
Did you guys hear about this?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.167
Apparently, former president
Trump's lawyers

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.200
just turned over more
classified items to the FBI

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.367
after finding them at
Trump's storage unit in Florida.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.901
Yeah, we were just
a week away from

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.567
our most classified secrets
ending up on

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.901
an episode of "Storage Wars."

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:52.100
I mean, really.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.634
A storage unit.
A storage unit.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.801
You know that you've stolen
too many top secret documents

00:01:56.801 --> 00:01:58.300
when you can't even fit them
all in your house.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.334
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:03.133
Meanwhile, last night, Trump
hosted an event at Mar-a-Lago

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:06.667
that featured a prominent
QAnon conspiracy theorist.

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:09.234
It's not good when you mingle
with a conspiracy theorist

00:02:09.234 --> 00:02:11.467
to distract from your dinner
with a white supremacist.

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.634
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.868
Switching gears, I saw
that TikTok just released

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:20.033
their 10 most popular videos
of 2022.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:21.734
And there's some
pretty cool videos in there.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:24.701
For example, the top video
was of a chocolatier making

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:25.868
a life-sized giraffe.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:26.901
Take a look at this.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:33.234
♪♪

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.534
Yeah, I mean,
that's impressive,

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.501
but, unfortunately, it bumped
this video off the list.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:42.033
-♪ Ahhhhh ♪

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.534
-Aah!
-What's going --

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:50.934
-Oh, my God!

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:53.734
-Another video in the top 10
was a remix of the corn kid.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:54.767
-Oh.
-Check this out.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.434
Yeah. That's great. It's cute.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:03.701
But, once again, that means that
this video got snubbed.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.300
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.100
Wow.

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:16.767
And, finally, Lizzo cracked
the top 10 for her video

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:18.834
where she shows the choreography
to "About Damn Time."

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:19.934
Here it is.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.534
-Feelin' fussy.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.501
Walkin' in my Balenci-ussies.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:26.934
-Yeah, that's right. Yeah.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:29.334
But, sadly, that knocked
this from the top 10.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.267
-Who painted the Mona Lisa?

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.767
Mona Lisa.
-Yeah.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:34.968
-Da Vinki?

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:36.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:41.667
-Better luck next year.
"Da Vinki?"

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:43.801
-"Da Vinki?"

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.067
-Hey, guys, get this --
airline passengers in Europe

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.267
will soon be allowed
to use 5G service

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.334
to make phone calls on board.

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:53.334
The only thing worse than your
seatmate trying to talk to you

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.167
is your seatmate
trying to talk to someone else.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.534
It's like,
"Hey, can you hear me?!

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.901
I'm on a plane right now!"

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.434
Yeah, this means no more putting
your phone on airplane mode.

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:04.701
Yep, everyone's like, "Finally,

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.834
we can stop pretending
to do that."

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:09.634
Good.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:10.834
Some entertainment news.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.868
"Wednesday" is on track
to become Netflix's

00:04:12.868 --> 00:04:16.300
most-watched English-language
TV series ever.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.234
You know these
are crazy times when a show

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:26.667
about a depressed goth child is
what makes us all happy.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.300
I mean...

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.100
It's good, it's good.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.501
Everyone's talking about
the holiday action movie

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.167
"Violent Night," as well.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.067
It did surprisingly well
at the box office,

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:41.634
so they're re-editing
old holiday favorites now

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.501
to capitalize on this new trend.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.400
-Really?
-Look at this ad I saw today.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:48.000
-They tried to take
everything he had,

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.701
but this Christmas,
George Bailey fights back.

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:54.534
He's smooth-talking,
hard-drinking,

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.868
and he's got a message
for anyone who crosses him.

00:04:56.868 --> 00:04:58.801
-You're going to die!
-[ Screams ]

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:05.100
-Every time a bell rings,
George kicks some ass.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.901
-Where's that money,
you stupid old [bleep]

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.601
-Wow.
-Wow!

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.501
"Stupid old --" beep!

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:20.300
-"Where's that money at?"

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.801
Right now, a lot of people are
putting out holiday decorations.

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:24.534
I saw one homeowner
in Wisconsin --

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:25.834
this made me laugh --
who kept it very simple.

00:05:25.834 --> 00:05:26.868
Look at this video.

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.501
♪♪
That's fantastic.

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:42.734
That's the most effort someone's
ever put into no effort.

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:45.200
-Guys, finally, we have
exactly eight shows left

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.400
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.434
for that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:52.434
It is time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters."

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.567
Here we go.

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:55.634
-♪ "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters" ♪

00:05:55.634 --> 00:06:00.534
♪ Eight days left ♪

00:06:00.534 --> 00:06:01.701
-That's right.

00:06:01.701 --> 00:06:05.133
Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:07.501
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.334
a heavenly Christmas sweater

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.133
from the "Countdown
to Christmas" cabinet.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.901
Since there are
eight shows left,

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:15.601
let's open door number 8,
shall we?

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:16.667
Hello.
-Hello.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.901
-This is it right here.

00:06:18.901 --> 00:06:20.434
I'm very excited about this one.
-It's a good one.

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:22.033
-Last one was hard to top.

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.434
The last one, we had someone's
head coming through a chimney.

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:25.534
-Exactly.
-Yeah. Here we go.

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.400
Let's see what we have tonight,
yeah.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.801 --> 00:06:35.667
♪♪

00:06:35.667 --> 00:06:36.934
Heavy.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:39.000
It's got some weight to it.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.200
Yeah.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.267
Wow.

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.701 --> 00:06:51.968
Epaulets?

00:06:51.968 --> 00:06:54.501
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:55.567
This is a heavy one.

00:06:55.567 --> 00:06:57.100
Everyone,
look at your seat number.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.968
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:06:59.968 --> 00:07:02.000
Quest, can I get a drumroll,
please?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.767
[ Drumroll ]

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:11.100
284!

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:19.133
♪♪

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:27.167
♪♪

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:29.501
Hey. I'm Jimmy.
Nice to see you.

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:31.467
Can you stand over there?

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.267
Welcome to the show.
What is your name?

00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:35.334
-Catalina.
-Catalina, where are you from?

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:36.968
-Portugal.
-Hey!

00:07:36.968 --> 00:07:38.267
Come on!

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:39.734
I'm so happy you're here.

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:41.601
-I'm happy, too.

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:45.000
-This is your color, basically.
-Yeah. It's my favorite color.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.267
-It just happened that pink
is your favorite color?

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:49.033
Do you have anything like this
in Portugal?

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:51.100
-No. I'm so happy.
-Yes.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:52.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:54.601
Well, you haven't
tried it on yet.

00:07:54.601 --> 00:07:56.667
-I'm sure it's going to be fine.

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:58.400
-Can you -- Can you try it on?

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.667
-Yeah, of course.
-Yeah?

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:01.667
Here you go.
It's got a lot of --

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:05.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.634 --> 00:08:07.734
No, okay, I can hear you.

00:08:07.734 --> 00:08:10.901
Catalina, oh.

00:08:10.901 --> 00:08:12.367
[ Laughs ]

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:13.467
Wow.

00:08:13.467 --> 00:08:15.300
Get your -- Oh --
You have -- Oh.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.501
Get your hair out.
You look gorgeous.

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:19.567
That's what I'm talking --
Look at that.

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:21.701
That's how you rock the sweater.

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.367
Beautiful!

00:08:23.367 --> 00:08:25.834
One more round of applause
for our winner.

00:08:25.834 --> 00:08:27.601
Congratulations.
Thank you for being here.

00:08:27.601 --> 00:08:28.901
Stick around.

00:08:28.901 --> 00:08:30.634
We'll be right back with
Michelle Pfeiffer, everybody.

00:08:30.634 --> 00:08:32.634
Come on back, now.

